  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum magnitude outcome of each lottery weighted by its probability, which corresponds to the expected value of the top outcome. The individual considers both the highest outcomes (2400 vs 2500) and their respective probabilities (34% vs 33%), and explicitly weighs the extra 100 Euros against the 1% lower chance. This aligns with evaluating the maximum outcome in relation to its probability, though the individual does not compute the exact weighted value. The justification centers on the same attributes—highest gain and its likelihood—and favors the higher gain despite a marginally lower probability, which is consistent with the rule of the decision reason. While the individual does not explicitly reference the concept of weighting the maximum outcome by probability, their reasoning pattern closely mirrors it. Therefore, it is highly likely the decision reason was used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 90
}

{
